 "title": "Government | Scott County, IN",
 "text": "Government | Scott County, IN\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nVA Temp Location\nVA Office temporary Location\nRead On...\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nDepartments\nGovernment\nResources\nServices\nHow Do I...\nSearch\nHome\nGovernment\nGovernment\n9\n1\n1\n2\nAgendas & Minutes\nAccess easily searchable meeting agendas and minutes for various boards, commissions, and committees.\nAssessor\nThe County Assessor is responsible for assessing the real and personal property within Scott County.\nAuditor\nThe Auditor’s office is a constitutional office and must wear many hats.\nBoards & Commissions\nView links to County boards and commissions along with their contact information. Lists of elected officials and departments are also available.\nClerk\nDiscover court fees and costs, useful links, and Clerk's Office news.\nCoroner\nSee contact information for the Coroner.\nCounty Commissioners\nLook at agendas, minutes, and videos, and learn about Commissioners.\nCounty Council\nRead about County Council members, as well as meeting materials.\nProsecutor\nFor more information regarding the Prosecutor's Office, please contact our office.\nRecorder\nThank you for visiting your online gateway to the Scott County Recorder’s Office. Here you will find information, forms, fees, requirements and many answers to your questions about recording documents and searching information.\nScott County Redevelopment Commission\nFind board members, meeting materials, and other information about the Scott County Redevelopment Commission.\nSurveyor\nThe County Surveyor must prepare, maintain and keep in their office a legal survey record book showing maps of sections, grants, subdivisions, or groups of such areas in sufficient detail so that the location of each is shown.\nTreasurer\nThe County Treasurer is the property tax collector and custodian of all monies with responsibility for investing idle funds and 